            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nThis behavior is expected since this is how `if ... then ... end` works here. Selecting `No` means that explorer will not be closed, hence the `MiniFiles.close()` returns `false` activating the `MiniFiles.open()` route. This example in the docs was chosen as it is because it works in most normal situations, is short, and (in its own sense) beautiful.\n\nThe more robust approach is something like this:\n\n```lua\nlocal minifiles_toggle = function(...)\n  if MiniFiles.get_explorer_state() then return MiniFiles.close() end\n  MiniFiles.open()\nend\n```\n\nMaybe it makes more sense to update to documentation, but the problem is that I really like the one-line solution that works most of the time. So I'll close this for now, but will keep this in mind.",
