            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Wow, I didn't expect to get a response this quick, thanks!\n\n> This behavior is expected since this is how `if ... then ... end` works here. Selecting `No` means that explorer will not be closed, hence the `MiniFiles.close()` returns `false` activating the `MiniFiles.open()` route.\n\nYeah, that makes perfect sense.\n\n> This example in the docs was chosen as it is because it works in most normal situations, is short, and (in its own sense) beautiful.\n\nRelatable! But I think I'll go with the robust alternative instead :D. Anyway, thanks for the help!\n\nEDIT: Or maybe the following? Not as elegant as the original docs example, though.\n\n```lua\nlocal minifiles_toggle = function(...) \n  if MiniFiles.close() == nil then MiniFiles.open(...) end \nend \n```",
